  "thumbnailAlt": "Church Membership form beside a photo of a smiling pastor greeting people seated in church pews",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A church membership form is a form that collects a person's contact and household details, faith background, baptism status, previous church and ministry interests so pastors and church staff can welcome them, plan a membership class and connect them to a team. This template lets one person register their whole household, asks gently about their faith journey, and ends with a commitment statement you can replace with your own covenant.",
    "audience": "Churches, parishes, chapels and faith communities of any size, plus church administrators, membership coordinators and pastors.",
    "useCases": [
      "Membership Sunday sign-ups after a newcomers' class",
      "A Join Us link in the weekly bulletin or church app",
      "Updating the church directory when families move or grow",
      "Parish registration for families moving into the area"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Put a QR code on the welcome card and the screens so people can join from their pew.",
      "Send new members to Google Sheets so ministry leaders see who picked their team.",
      "Turn on the email copy to the respondent so each new member gets a note with your next membership class."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a church membership form include?",
        "answer": "Name, contact details and address, household members and children's birthdates, how long they have attended, faith background and baptism status, previous church, interest in a membership class, ministries they would like to serve in, permission for the church directory, and a statement of faith or covenant."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do people have to be baptized to become members?",
        "answer": "It depends on the church and denomination. Many require baptism or a profession of faith, while others welcome people as they prepare for it; adjust the question to match your own rules."
      },
      {
        "question": "How should a church protect members' personal information?",
        "answer": "Collect only what you use, limit access to staff who need it, and ask before publishing anyone in a directory. Data protection rules for charities and churches vary by country, so check your local requirements."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can one person register a whole family?",
        "answer": "Yes. The form has space to list spouses and children, so one adult can register the household in one go."
      }
    ]
  },
